hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1493","Issa bin Ibrahim Al-Ghafiqi Al-Misri narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, that Abu Yunus, and he was Sulaym bin Jubayr He narrated to him, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Every soul is prescribed to give alms every day on which the sun rises. That is: To do justice between two people is a charity, and to help a man on his animal and carry him on it is a charity, and to remove harmful things from the road is a charity. That is to help a man on his mount and carry him on it, and to lift his belongings onto it is a charity, and a kind word is a charity, and every step you take is a charity. Thereby, to prayer is charity.”"
"1494","Al-Hussein told us, Ibn Al-Mubarak told us, Muammar told us, on the authority of Hammam bin Munabbih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said: “A good word is a charity, and every step you take towards prayer is a charity.”"
